    "updated_at": "2018-03-21T16:27:40Z",
    "body": "I've thought about it, since it definitely would make our chrome implementation a lot simpler (for a very long time we had a bug where transferring a closed message port would magically re-open it). No idea why ports were specified to behave the way they do. I do wonder how web compatible this change is? Of course there is not much point in transferring closed ports, but throwing where before we didn't throw might still cause sites to break...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
